<HelloFraandsPage title="Use it in a healthy way" summary="Baat karo, dil halka karo — par apna khayal pehle." review={false} related={[]}>
<p>{BRAND.name} is for friendly conversation: someone to talk to after a long day, before an exam, or when you feel alone. It works best as <strong>one good thing in your life</strong>, not the only one. This page explains how we keep it healthy for callers and hosts.</p>
<h2>Hosts are friends, not partners</h2>
<p>Hosts are real, independent people who offer friendly conversation. They are not your girlfriend or boyfriend, and this is not a dating or relationship service. A host being kind to you on a call is their job done well — it is not a promise of love or a future together.</p>
<ul><li>Hosts will not flirt, say "I love you", share their number or meet you.</li><li>Asking a host for these things can lead to a strike.</li><li>If you notice you are thinking about one host all the time, take a break and talk to people around you too.</li></ul>
<h2>Healthy limits</h2>
<p>To protect callers and hosts, the service will include limits when calling launches:</p>
<ul><li><strong>Time with one host:</strong> a daily limit on minutes with the same host, and a short cooling-off gap before calling them again.</li><li><strong>Daily spending limit:</strong> a cap on how much you can spend in a day, and an extra check before a large top-up.</li><li><strong>Gentle reminders</strong> if calls with one host become very long or very frequent.</li></ul>
<p>When a limit applies, you will simply see <em>"This host isn't available right now."</em> It does not mean the host is angry with you or has rejected you. It is a platform rule, the same for everyone.</p>
<h2>If you feel very low</h2>
<p>Hosts are not counsellors and this is not a crisis service. If you feel hopeless, think about hurting yourself, or feel you cannot go on, please talk to trained people now:</p>
<ul><li><a href="tel:14416">Tele-MANAS 14416</a> — free mental-health support, 24×7, in many Indian languages.</li><li><a href="tel:112">112</a> — if you or someone else is in danger.</li></ul>
<p>More numbers are on our <a href="/emergency">emergency support</a> page. Telling a host how you feel is never a reason for a strike. A host may share these numbers with you and end the call so you can get real help. That is care, not rejection.</p>
<h2>Money and time</h2>
<p>Only spend what you can afford. Calls are paid per minute and are not refunded, so set yourself a budget. Unused wallet money is always yours — you can send it back to your UPI ID at any time.</p>
<h2>For hosts</h2>
<p>Hosts follow our <a href="/hosts/crisis-script">welfare and crisis guide</a>: they spot signs of distress and attachment, share the right helpline, keep clear boundaries, and flag concerns so the platform — not the host — limits contact when needed.</p>
</HelloFraandsPage>
